From f0b6f0579c3fab7082f70218292b1079cdcbed84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:42:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH net v6 0/5] bpf, sockmap: fix copied_seq receive ordering

Sockmap stream verdict can process TCP data after userspace has
already consumed part of an skb. The current copied_seq accounting can
then count bytes that were already read, or can advance over earlier
SK_PASS data that is still queued on psock->ingress_msg.

Both cases can move copied_seq beyond rcv_nxt and make later native TCP
receive hit the tcp_recvmsg_locked() sequence warning.

Patch 1 makes tcp_eat_skb() account only unread receive sequence.
Patch 2 trims self-ingress SK_PASS data by copied_seq in both the
direct ingress path and queued backlog path.
Patch 3 defers later skipped receive sequence behind an earlier unread
self-ingress SK_PASS message.
Patch 4 accounts pending self-ingress sequence after stopping sockmap
callbacks and before psock detach, while leaving queue release in the
RCU destroy work.
Patch 5 adds sockmap_basic regression coverage for those paths.

v6:
  - Split the previous copied_seq receive-ordering patch into three
    focused patches: SK_PASS range trimming, deferred skipped-sequence
    accounting, and detach-time pending sequence accounting.
  - Mark local SK_PASS skbs with a sockmap-private self-ingress bit, so
    trimming and detach accounting do not depend on skb owner state.
  - Clarify that backlog range trimming only applies to self-ingress TCP
    skbs; redirected ingress skbs keep their original range.
  - Stop installed sockmap callbacks before detach-time pending sequence
    accounting, closing a race with late verdict processing.
  - Use u32 for deferred skipped-sequence accounting.

Dong Chenchen (5):
  bpf, sockmap: account only unread data in tcp_eat_skb
  bpf, sockmap: trim self-ingress SK_PASS by copied_seq
  bpf, sockmap: defer skipped receive sequence behind SK_PASS
  bpf, sockmap: account pending self-ingress before detach
  selftests/bpf: cover sockmap TCP receive sequence handling

